WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Zero kara kakedashite

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.130
Start running from the beginning,

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
Omoi dake wo dakishimete

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:08.500
with nothing but your emotions in your hands.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Sonomama kakenukete

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.890
Just keep running...

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
Itsumo koko de mitsumeteru

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:18.350
I'm always watching you from here.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
Hajimete deatta hi no manazashi wasurenai

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:42.300
I still remember your expression the day we first met.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
Taiyou mitai ni kokoro wo terashitekureta

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:49.190
It lit up my heart like the sun.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
Asu no yukue sagashite nayandeiru nara

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:56.960
If you're anxious about where to go tomorrow,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
Ima kimi no tame ni akari ni naritai yo

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:06.890
I want to become a beacon to you.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Zero kara tobidatte

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.010
Start flying from the beginning.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Ima no kimi wo toki hanachi

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:16.380
Let go of your current self...

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
Mugen ni habataite

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.730
and fly towards infinity.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Donna toki mo mimaru yo

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:23.600
I will always watch over you...

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
Kitto zutto tooku made

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.510
no matter how far you fly.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:38.000
<i>The Two Princesses</i> is approaching its final show after a hugely successful run.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.480
This is the first time Ayumi has ever experienced a complete transformation into her character on stage,

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:49.960
which is why she was so shocked when Maya told her she thought it was normal.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:56.130
Episode 39 - The Purple Shadow

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:03.350
A starring role on a TV show and Ophelia in <i>Hamlet</i>. They're both good offers.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.550
It's amazing, Maya.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:08.200
But you know, Maya, if you want to grab that award,

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.460
you have to pick a role worthy of you.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:13.050
A role worthy of me...

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:19.850
What am I doing, standing out here like this?

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:21.510
All for that girl...

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:26.800
Do you have any idea how important the person you're meeting is to Daito Entertainment?

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:30.900
You will obey me, Masumi.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:33.460
Maya.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.510
I'm off to the store!

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:40.810
Mr. Hayami!

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.000
I have a favor to ask of you, little one.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.740
What are you plotting this time?!

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:46.650
Plotting?

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:50.240
Well, that's what you normally get up to, isn't it?

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:52.020
It's nothing bad.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.630
Will you come with me for a bit?

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:55.400
Please.

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:17.250
I used to come here all the time when I was a kid.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.810
I liked its vast, empty spaces.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:25.700
When I came here, all my troubles seemed so insignificant, no matter what they were.

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.740
It's like we're floating in space.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.690
How small we are!

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:33.850
It's overwhelming!

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:36.030
It's so breathtaking!

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:47.310
Thanks for taking this nostalgic little trip with me.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.860
No problem.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:53.810
Well, if it isn't young Hayami!

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.770
Hello, sir. You look like you're in good spirits.

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:59.200
This is even more impressive than before!

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.340
I'm going to take a look at the projector.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:06.380
He used to come here a lot by himself when he was little.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:08.940
He would often be on the verge of tears.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:13.420
After he lost his mother, he would sit in a corner, crying softly to himself.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.200
I can't really imagine him of all people... crying in a corner.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.660
You're the first person he's ever brought here.

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:29.380
It's been years. I used to come here a lot.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:33.910
I can't really imagine you as a child.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:35.570
That's a horrible thing to say!

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:38.210
I was a good kid: obedient and mature.

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:41.560
So, I guess it all went wrong later on, then.

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:43.560
Maybe so.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.680
Masumi, don't show your good-natured side to anyone.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:51.160
If someone approaches you with a smile, you need to be on your toes.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.460
Keep your fangs sharp at all times!

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:01.450
It's a lost child! What should we do?

00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:04.290
It's going to be hard to find his parents in this crowd.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:13.300
Yes, just like that. Now, let it all out, good and loud!

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.170
Mom!

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:15.950
Mom!

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.600
Mr. Hayami...

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:24.720
Bye!

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:26.770
See you later!

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:29.430
Sometimes, I really don't understand you.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:34.370
I think you might actually be a really caring person after all.

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:42.040
Are you bored?

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.310
You're so quiet.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:46.180
No, of course not.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:50.800
What exactly am I trying to do here?!

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:56.520
I'm afraid of this girl's reaction... of her rejection.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:06:01.630
Yet, all I have to do is mention purple roses.

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:04.720
So, why is it so hard?

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:12.530
Please... tell me. What's with the kind glint I sometimes catch sight of in your eyes?

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:16.460
Why do your eyes look so lonely?

00:06:16.460 --> 00:06:19.030
Won't you tell me what you're thinking?

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:31.170
The reason I asked you to come here with me today is because I...

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:34.920
Excuse me a moment.

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:38.330
Hello?

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:41.920
What? Ms. Tsukikage has gone missing?!

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.500
She left a letter?

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:52.050
I'm going to rest up somewhere secluded until I am better.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.270
I know I will return someday.

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:57.780
Maya, I'll be watching you from afar.

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:00.650
Stay strong, no matter what life throws at you.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:05.180
Why didn't she tell me she was in such shape?

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:07.870
She's not seriously ill.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:10.080
It's just that this was the first time she's been on stage in a while...

00:07:10.080 --> 00:07:11.640
and she needs some time to recover.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:14.570
Don't worry. We'll find her.

00:07:14.570 --> 00:07:15.890
You will, won't you?

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:21.350
If she ends up like my mother, I'll never, ever forgive you!

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:24.640
Give me back my mother!

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:30.170
I wanted to wait until she was an adult.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:35.420
But I can't expect her to ever forgive me.

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:39.070
I have no choice but to remain in the shadows forever.

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:47.680
There's always a red light between me and her, and I can never cross over to her.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:52.700
Yes, Father. I've decided.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.430
I agree to your wish for an arranged marriage.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:57.500
The Two Princesses

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:03.440
I know she's here somewhere.

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:07.550
Where? Where's the actress I'm looking for?

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:14.510
The eyes of an actress!

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.510
There! There she is!

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.510
Then, let's go!

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:24.670
I want to act again.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:27.500
I don't know what role to choose, though.

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:31.230
That was a real hit! We deserve a drink!

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:33.490
Maya Kitajima.

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:38.350
Ryuuzo Kuronuma.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:40.870
You're the Miss Kitajima that played Aldis, correct?

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:42.390
Yes, that's right.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:44.570
I like your eyes.

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:45.880
They're perfect.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:49.390
Will you act in my next play?

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:54.980
You won't be playing a human, but instead, you'll play a girl raised by wolves.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:08:56.910
A wolf girl.

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:00.200
A wolf girl.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:03.530
Jane is a girl raised by wolves...

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:06.770
ever since she was a baby and she regards herself as a wolf.

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:10.790
She is captured by humans, made into a freak show...

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:13.810
and reminisces about the family she has been torn away from.

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:15.270
And then...

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:24.530
I want to do it. I want to play Jane!

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:32.460
I have to choose a role that best suits me - a role I can really sink my teeth into.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:35.080
There isn't much time left until the casting for <i>The Scarlet Angel</i>,

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:38.030
and if I don't win an award for this role...

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:42.650
I'll put all my chips on Jane, the wolf girl!

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:51.900
I knew you'd come, Miss Kitajima.

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:54.530
Thank you for having me!

00:09:57.930 --> 00:09:59.810
This is a piece of meat!

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:03.510
Take it from me as though you're a wolf!

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:07.610
A wolf. Now, I must become a wolf.

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:10.340
That's a piece of meat.

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:12.600
Hey!

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:50.510
Come on, then!

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:20.230
Stop right there.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:25.630
Thank you.

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:30.840
I'm sorry I hit you, but you were really coming at me.

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:35.480
They're wild, barbaric, and they kill without hesitation.

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:38.520
Yet, wolves reputedly possess more than that.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.860
I want you to make us feel that extra something.

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:46.590
The next time I see you, I'd like you to express joy, rage, sadness and fun, as a wolf.

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:50.020
Joy, rage, sadness and fun... as a wolf?

00:12:11.050 --> 00:12:13.220
I thought I'd lost that hair clip.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:18.520
I'm looking at ordinary objects in a new way.

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:22.740
How do humans see Jane?

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:28.820
How does it feel to be forced to walk on two legs, sit on a chair and made to speak?

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:31.540
A harsh and cruel world...

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:36.710
But there is one person. Stewart.

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:41.630
Acting with Stewart will be hardest of all.

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:43.850
I wonder what kind of person will be playing him.

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:48.350
Mr. Hayami!

00:12:49.340 --> 00:12:51.740
You're looking well, Maya!

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:52.920
Miss Mizuki!

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:56.310
Who was that woman with Mr. Hayami just now?

00:12:59.040 --> 00:13:00.980
She is a prospective arranged marriage partner.

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:05.720
An arranged marriage?

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:09.240
He's getting married? Is that why he was smiling?

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:12.250
So is it already all...

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.800
Nothing has been decided yet.

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:17.720
But it's just a matter of time.

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:20.540
What's this feeling?

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:24.780
It feels like my heart... just emptied itself.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.430
I will now announce the roles.

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:33.590
The part of Jane, the wolf girl, will be played by Maya Kitajima.

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:39.320
And the part of Stewart will be played by...

00:13:39.980 --> 00:13:41.840
Yuu Sakurakouji.

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:44.090
Sakurakouji!

00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:47.040
Good job, everyone!

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.540
Well, um...

00:13:56.270 --> 00:14:01.640
You remember I said I always wanted to act on stage with you?

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:05.530
Yeah, I remember.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:08.930
I want to play off your character.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:12.070
Yeah, I really want to make this into a great show.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:16.600
Mai...

00:14:17.590 --> 00:14:18.870
Let me introduce you.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.790
This is Maya Kitajima.

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.990
Hello! Nice to meet you!

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:25.150
And this is a girl from my acting troupe, Mai Asou.

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:26.470
I've been waiting for you.

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:27.700
What?

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:30.350
You said we were going to grab a bite to eat together.

00:14:31.440 --> 00:14:34.020
I'll catch you in rehearsals!

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:38.230
Why did you lie?

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:40.890
We didn't make any plans to eat out.

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:43.090
Tell me the truth...

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:47.460
Did you try out for this play because Kitajima was in it?

00:14:48.060 --> 00:14:50.100
I know about what happened.

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:52.790
Do you still love her?

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:55.460
She's a rival now.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:15:00.090
I tried out for this play because I liked the concept.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:03.680
He has a pretty girlfriend.

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:07.130
It was kinda sad, but also a relief...

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:12.100
Time does strange things to people.
People's hearts can change their fates.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:14.500
"Are wedding bells in the air?!"

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.480
Mr. Hayami is getting married?

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:19.710
Hayami here.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:22.220
Hello? This is Hayami.

00:15:22.220 --> 00:15:24.460
Um, it's me. Kitajima.

00:15:24.850 --> 00:15:27.930
I'm playing a wolf girl in my next play!

00:15:27.930 --> 00:15:30.270
No. What on earth am I saying?!

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:31.360
Wow, really?

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:33.380
That role sounds <i>perfect</i> for you.

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:34.980
I'm looking forward to seeing you in it.

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:39.010
Um, well...

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:43.120
What is it? Do you have something to say?

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.500
No... I hope you'll be very happy!

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:49.230
What's that supposed to mean?

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:53.710
What on earth am I doing?

00:15:55.830 --> 00:15:57.830
It's not like it matters anyway!

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:01.310
It doesn't matter.

00:16:02.410 --> 00:16:06.560
We would like very much for an award to come our way this time around.

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:09.690
We appointed you with that in mind.

00:16:09.690 --> 00:16:12.500
I am not doing this for mere awards.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:14.730
I want to put on a show that's truly alive.

00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:18.190
I do not create my scenes to be used as tabloid fodder!

00:16:19.760 --> 00:16:22.230
Okay, let's take it from the pack leader's howl.

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:27.650
The curtain has gone up, but the stage remains pitch black.

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:31.710
This is how the audience first hears the howl of a wolf.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:35.140
Howl, Jane!

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:41.900
No, that's not it.

00:16:44.060 --> 00:16:48.900
No! This first noise ties the whole play together; it's the sound of Jane's soul!

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:52.390
The first sound is the sound of Jane's soul.

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:56.220
Her separation from the familiar wilderness and her family...

00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:58.730
her capture by the two-legged beasts.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:01.690
No, no! You have to capture Jane's soul!

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:07.820
I'm so alone... Mother! Father!

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:23.330
That's the one!

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:24.350
Don't forget that last howl.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:25.780
Jane.

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:28.870
Now, you're in the wilderness and for the first time,

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:30.890
a huge enemy looms over you.

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:38.340
What's this?

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:40.750
I'm scared... Really scared!

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:49.490
Next scene!

00:17:51.390 --> 00:17:52.780
Stewart!

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:59.060
Don't be afraid.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:00.830
It's meat.

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:02.490
You can have some if you like.

00:18:14.850 --> 00:18:15.870
Next scene!

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:29.600
This is a cage!

00:18:33.730 --> 00:18:37.570
I'm scared... Humans are scary!

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:39.140
She's scared.

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:40.270
She's really terrified!

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:45.630
All right. You can become human again, Kitajima.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:57.350
Being treated like Jane has taught her how to capture Jane's essence.

00:18:57.350 --> 00:19:00.060
I knew she was the right girl for the part!

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:10.560
That's Ryuuzo Kuronuma. He's doing <i>The Wolf Girl</i> at the Osawa Theater for his next show.

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:13.150
All I ask is that you're nice to them, Kuronuma.

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:16.990
If you get chummy with the judges from the acting competition here tonight...

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:18.800
You're Mr. Kuronuma, right?

00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:24.830
It must be hard putting on <i>The Wolf Girl</i>.

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:28.680
I feel that directing a show is much like conducting an orchestra.

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:30.660
The actors are the instruments.

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:33.490
To put on a great performance, you need great instruments.

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:38.610
I've searched long and hard for the perfect instrument to play the wolf girl.

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:39.940
I don't doubt that.

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:43.920
Wasn't she acting with Daito until recently?

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:46.160
Don't worry about that.

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:49.720
But you have very good taste if you picked out Maya Kitajima yourself.

00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:52.860
Then, I'll take my leave for now.

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:55.760
You know, you're not as much of a jerk as the rumors make you out to be.

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:59.610
I wonder why you let her go.

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:02.670
Maya Kitajima, I mean!

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:07.250
Mr. Hayami, you supposedly have very good taste as well.

00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:11.840
Nothing's changed, Mr. Masumi.

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:13.380
What are you talking about?

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:15.880
The intended recipient of this purple rose.

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:18.630
This time she's playing a wolf girl.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:22.420
You're always thinking about her, aren't you?

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:26.510
Mr. Masumi, the light between you won't always be red.

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:31.410
What do you mean by that, Miss Mizuki?

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:43.090
I guess you still love hamburgers, don't you, Maya?

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:48.010
Why am I blushing? Is it because the way he says my name reminds me of old times?

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:50.780
You really transform into a completely different person when you're playing Jane.

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:53.550
I can't believe it's the same person who played Princess Aldis.

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:55.370
You saw that play?

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:58.690
Yeah. I mean, it looked interesting.

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:01.000
Your <i>A Midsummer Night's Dream</i> was good too.

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:07.020
He's been following my progress this whole time.

00:21:09.170 --> 00:21:11.010
The train's here!

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:12.750
Maya, hurry!

00:21:13.440 --> 00:21:15.280
Sakurakouji!

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:20.440
This isn't Stewart's hand. It's Sakurakouji's.

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:27.290
Let's make this a great show. I won't lose.

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:34.000
I won't lose either, Sakurakouji.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:35.730
On stage, we're rivals.

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:37.400
Maya.

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:42.870
The rigorous role of the wolf girl; the reappearance of Sakurakouji as a co-star;

00:21:42.870 --> 00:21:47.200
and now, the fact that Masumi Hayami has a girlfriend have all contributed to the confusion...

00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:50.010
swirling around inside Maya's head.

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:18.080
Chikazukitai noni toozaketeshimau

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:18.080
I want to be close to you, but you're distancing yourself.

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:31.320
Dakishimetai toki wazato hanareteshimau

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:31.320
When I want to hold you, you deliberately run away.

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:44.070
Marude jishaku no N to N no you da ne

00:22:31.320 --> 00:22:44.070
We're like two poles on a magnet...

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:55.190
Otagai amari nimo nisugita seikana?

00:22:44.070 --> 00:22:55.190
Maybe we're too alike?

00:22:55.190 --> 00:23:09.920
Motto motto sunao na hitomi de mitsureba

00:22:55.190 --> 00:23:09.920
If you allow your eyes to see the truth,

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:21.510
Yodonderu izumi mo suki tooru hazusa

00:23:09.920 --> 00:23:21.510
even quagmires will become crystal clear.

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:29.320
Maya, you haven't changed a bit, but you've really grown as an actor.

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:33.830
I've been working hard so that we can be on the same stage.

00:23:34.770 --> 00:23:39.150
The day has finally come, but now, another play has taken away our rehearsal space,

00:23:39.150 --> 00:23:41.570
and we've lost our costars.

00:23:42.820 --> 00:23:47.440
Will we be able to perform <i>The Forgotten Wilderness</i>?

00:23:46.080 --> 00:23:51.500
Episode 40 - Jane, the Wolf Girl
